{
  "id": "path-study-success",
  "title": "Study success — path analysis with observed variables (SYNTHETIC)",
  "summary": "Background (SES, prior GPA) predicts motivation, motivation predicts study hours, and all three feed the exam score. Five observed variables, no latent constructs. Synthetic data (N = 400).",
  "theory": "Path analysis (Wright, 1934; Kline, 2016, ch. 7) applied to a generic expectancy-value view of student achievement. The model is a teaching illustration, not a published theory.",
  "modelNote": "An over-identified recursive path model: three paths are deliberately left out (SES → study hours, prior GPA → study hours, SES → exam score), so CB-SEM has 3 degrees of freedom and the fit indices test those restrictions. Indirect effects run through motivation and study hours.",
  "scaleSource": "SES is a standardised index; prior GPA 1–5; motivation is a 1–7 item mean; study hours per week; exam score 0–100.",
  "dataset": {
